================ 4. minimal :283 repro vs control (waves probe) ================
METHOD    identical hermetic fixture trees (pgrep/journal/df/tmux stubs, one
          unsettled wave dir with a nested subdir); the ONLY difference is
          chmod 000 on the nested subdir. Repro rc=1 with the header line only
          and NO MORI_CENSUS verdict; control rc=0, full 7-surface run, CLEAN.
          find on an unreadable subdir = rc 1 (measured; stderr dropped as the
          :283 construct does), so the pipefail assignment at
          tools/mori-census.sh:283 aborts the run under set -e.
CLOCK     2026-10-15T16:49:31Z; census sha e3073a2b… (unchanged).
FIND_RC   find rc=1; stderr: find: '…/sub': Permission denied
RECIPE (/tmp only; control = same fixture without the chmod):
  D=$(mktemp -d /tmp/mori-r283.XXXXXX); mkdir -p "$D/bin" "$D/ufo/waves/wave-locked/locked" "$D/ufo/state" "$D/root"
  # stubs (+x): pgrep prints '1234 bash /path/scripts/shokunin-watchdog.sh'; journal exits 0;
  #            df prints 'Filesystem …\n/dev/fx 1000000 10000 990000 2%% /fx'; tmux prints one line
  printf '{}\n' > "$D/ufo/waves/wave-locked/swarm-registry.json"; printf '{}\n' > "$D/ufo/waves/wave-locked/dispatch.json"
  printf '%s tick=1\n' "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S+00:00)" > "$D/ufo/watchdog.log"; touch "$D/ufo/watchdog.log"; printf '1\n' > "$D/ufo/state/kagi.round"
  chmod 000 "$D/ufo/waves/wave-locked/locked"   # the ONLY difference vs control
  env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin HOME="$D" LC_ALL=C TZ=UTC MORI_SHOKUNIN_ROOT="$D/root" MORI_UFO_DIR="$D/ufo" \
    MORI_WATCHDOG_LOG="$D/ufo/watchdog.log" MORI_STATE_DIR="$D/ufo/state" MORI_WAVES_DIR="$D/ufo/waves" \
    MORI_DISK_TARGETS="$D/root" MORI_PGREP_BIN="$D/bin/pgrep" MORI_JOURNALCTL_BIN="$D/bin/journal" \
    MORI_DF_BIN="$D/bin/df" MORI_TMUX_BIN="$D/bin/tmux" MORI_ROSTER_LANES="no-such-lane" MORI_NOW_EPOCH="$(date +%s)" \
    bash tools/mori-census.sh ; echo "rc=$?"
